== 20. Open Decisions Before Adoption ==
To be resolved (ideally with retained Swiss counsel) before this policy is set effective.
1. Delete or appropriately minimize the historical FactHarbor documentation-analytics records and document completion; keep audience analytics disabled unless a separately reviewed lawful design is adopted (§4.2, §7, §10).
2. Re-verify current alpha exposure and submitted-data inventory. The 2026-06-11 count is historical and must not be treated as current.
3. Publish and set this policy effective before widening access and confirm the competent Verein approval (§2, §19).
4. Confirm the lawful basis, especially for sensitive-data handling and the deliberate publication of full submissions and reports (§3.3, §6).
5. Complete the per-provider matrix — role (processor vs independent controller), transfer mechanism (DPF/SCC), configured retention/training settings, and current service terms for Anthropic, OpenAI, Serper/Google, Wikipedia, GitHub, Cloudflare/cdnjs, Google Fonts, Infomaniak and optional providers (§4–5, §13.1).
6. Decide whether EU/EEA users are in scope and, if so, complete the GDPR Art. 6/9 analysis and appoint an EU representative under Art. 27 (§11.5).
7. Set a submission **retention cap**, deletion workflow/SLA and backup-deletion propagation (§7, §9).
8. Verify production-hosting location, host-log fields/retention, backup retention and infrastructure-processor disclosure (§4.2, §7, §11.1).
9. Complete an initial DPIA now, a full DPIA before wider public launch, and the processing-activities register (§11.3, §11.4).
10. Implement the **personality-rights / takedown workflow** for reports about identifiable persons (§6.2) and the source-excerpt/copyright safeguards (§5.3).
11. Decide whether to require pre-submission click-through acceptance (see Terms of Service §1) rather than relying on browsewrap for the liability, indemnity, visibility and transfer clauses. The visible Privacy Policy and Terms links are already present at the collection point.

